  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Isolated single-layer MoE CUDA Graph replay with pre-quantized inputs and capacity 256; does not measure end-to-end TPOT/TTFT inside a full serving engine or prefill workloads (where 128 compute SMs become the bottleneck).",
    "Section 8 explicitly omits both a controlled partition-size (dispatch_sms) sweep and an overlap-on/off ablation in v1, so Green-Context overlap, K128 weight prepacking, and tag-2 removal gains are not separately decomposed.",
    "H20 baseline uses an author-written SM90 reference port (sm90_fp8_fp4_mega_moe) because public DeepGEMM 2.8.2 ships SM100 only, and the H20 shared-expert baseline runs two unfused kernels (1.188x vs unfused Mega vs 1.123x feature-matched on B300).",
    "Hard Appendix A Table 12 constraints: I <= 4096 (mod 128), H mod 256 = 0, k + 1[shared] <= 32, E <= 2048 global (<= 512/rank, E mod P = 0), P <= 72 ranks, routed (1,1,32) SwiGLU only, single process per peer-accessible GPU, and serialized calls per single-instance workspace.",
    "HBM working-set bandwidth and NVLink payload bandwidth in Table 9 are analytic models rather than hardware PMU counters."
  ],
